{"id":"dcyf-pages-against-payments","title":"Youth grants: what the City paid on each 2024-29 agreement against what the grantee's pages report","question":"Did the City pay any youth grantee more on its 2024-29 agreements than its program pages say it spent, and how much of the department's money to nonprofits went to payees with a program page?","finding":"131 payees hold 2024-29 agreements that match program pages. Under the fiscal 2025 and 2026 labels they were paid $178.7 million against $208.8 million of spending their pages report for 2024-25 and 2025-26 (0.86 times); none were paid more than 5% above it once fiscally sponsored programs are counted with their sponsor. Of $115.2 million the department paid nonprofit-flagged payees in fiscal 2026, $105.0 million (91%) went to payees with a program page; the largest without one is City College Of San Francisco ($9.5 million).","how":"Every voucher line of department CHF whose agreement title carries \"24-29\" was summed by agreement and label year. A payee is joined to the grantee names on the pages by name (hotspots.norm, plus the payee spellings in PAYEE_ALIAS); a fiscal sponsor's agreement is joined to the program its title names (SPONSORED, checked by hand). Reported spending is the Expenditures figure on each program page.","limits":"Payments lag spending: claims for the last months of 2025-26 are paid under the fiscal 2027 label, so paid-to-reported below 1 is expected and is not money missing. A name join can miss a payee spelled differently; such payees appear in the uncovered list rather than being dropped. City College of San Francisco is flagged as a nonprofit in the payment table; its payments are a memorandum of understanding (Free City), not a grant with a page.","tier":"CLEARED","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Grantee","type":"org"},{"k":"payee","t":"City payee","type":"text"},{"k":"agreements","t":"2024-29 agreements","type":"int"},{"k":"programs","t":"Program pages","type":"int"},{"k":"paid2025_26","